     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 2400 mg four times daily is 9,600 mg/day. That is three times the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. Ibuprofen's analgesic and anti-inflammatory effect plateaus well below that dose. Above it you mainly add risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and metabolic toxicity, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the maximum dose, I'd suggest talking with pharmacy or clinical toxicology first. For more analgesia, a multimodal regimen may work better than a higher ibuprofen dose. That could mean adding scheduled acetaminophen or another agent.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to enter?"
      }
     ],
